## Current Codex routing rule

Route Luna Low/Medium to clear repeatable extraction, Terra Medium/Standard to
routine reasoning, Terra/Sol High to difficult repair, and Sol High/XHigh to
protocol/cross-system risk. Sol Max is one hardest sequential task. Sol/Terra
Ultra requires independent scopes, stop conditions, and fuel justification;
Luna Ultra is unsupported by the dated local snapshot.


## v3.9.3 Auto/Max explicit boundary

Auto is not a specific model. For OPTION-PROFIT controlled work, do not recommend Auto as the default route unless the owner explicitly accepts non-deterministic provider/model routing for low-risk exploration.

Max Mode is a separate Cursor-level capacity toggle for explicit models except Auto. Keep Max OFF by default; recommend 1M/Max only with context-overflow, broad-audit, large multimodal context, or explicit owner approval.

## v3.9.3 model/mode routing rule

When recommending model/settings, use the dated provider snapshot. Do not recommend the strongest model by default.

- Cursor Agent: Composer 2.5 remains the generic default for clear scoped implementation, but exact current model controls require refreshed Cursor evidence.
- Auto: not default for controlled OPTION-PROFIT work.
- Max/1M: capacity only; off unless context-overflow/broad-audit/owner approval.
- Ask: read-only. Plan: pre-apply. Debug: evidence-first. Multitask: only independent scoped tasks.
- ChatGPT desktop Codex, Codex IDE extension, Codex CLI, Codex web, GPT web, and Cursor Agent are distinct surfaces. Cursor Max Mode is capacity; Codex Max and Ultra are alternative reasoning-effort choices. Owner-facing ChatGPT Codex tuples contain only surface, model, reasoning, and speed.
- Standard is the default speed. Fast is latency-first/increased-usage; no fixed GPT-5.6 public multiplier is established.
